---
import DraftNotice from "~/components/DraftNotice.astro";
import LegalSection from "~/components/LegalSection.astro";
import PageHeader from "~/components/PageHeader.astro";
import Section from "~/components/Section.astro";
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import {
  formatMoney,
  formatPriceRate,
  formatSharePercent,
  site,
  supportEmailUrl,
} from "~/config/site";

const version = "0.2";
const updated = "2026-10-25";

// Before this page ships, the site owner still has to supply (kept here, not
// shown on the page):
//  - The legal entity name, its registered address, the country whose law governs these terms and the courts that hear a dispute.
//  - The liability cap. This draft uses the fees paid in the 12 months before a claim.
//  - Whether tax is added to top-ups, and whether refunds work differently for consumers anywhere.

const name = site.name;
const minimumCallBalance = formatMoney(site.pricing.minimumCallBalance);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for using the hosted product. This page is a first draft awaiting review."
  noindex
>
  <PageHeader
    label="Terms"
    heading="Terms"
    lede={`The agreement between you and ${name} for using the hosted product.`}
  >
    <DraftNotice version={version} updated={updated} />
  </PageHeader>

  <Section label="The terms" filled>
    <div class="ruled">
      <LegalSection heading="Who we are">
        <p>
          {`${name} is a hosted platform for building AI voice agents that answer and place phone calls. In these terms "we" means ${name}, and "you" means the person or business using it. By creating an account you accept these terms.`}
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions about them go to <a href={supportEmailUrl} class="link">{site.supportEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Accounts and workspaces">
        <p>
          You need an account to use the service. Give a working email address
          and keep your sign-in to yourself. You are responsible for what is
          done with your account.
        </p>
        <p>
          Agents, phone numbers, recordings and credit belong to a workspace. A
          workspace can have several members. Its owner and admins manage its
          settings and keys, and the owner adds credit. If you invite someone to
          a workspace, you are responsible for what they do in it.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Prepaid credit">
        <p>
          {`${name} is prepaid. Each workspace has a balance in ${site.pricing.currency}. Calls are charged at ${formatPriceRate()} of call time, counted by the second; part of a second counts as a whole one. A new call needs a minimum balance to start, currently ${minimumCallBalance}. There is no free credit.`}
        </p>
        <p>
          You top up by card through Stripe, within the amounts shown on the
          Billing page. Stripe handles the payment, and your card details stay
          with Stripe.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Automatic top-up">
        <p>
          {`If you save a card and turn on automatic top-up, you authorise ${name} to charge that card the amount you choose whenever your workspace's balance drops below the threshold you set, up to five times in any 24 hours. Automatic top-ups are prepaid credit on the same terms as other top-ups.`}
        </p>
        <p>
          You can change the amounts, turn automatic top-up off or remove the
          card at any time in Billing. If a charge fails, we turn automatic
          top-up off and email you.
        </p>
        <p>
          {`Your card is stored by Stripe; ${name} keeps only its brand, last four digits and expiry.`}
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Unused credit and refunds">
        <p>
          Unused credit stays in its workspace while the account is open. It is
          not cash and cannot be moved to another workspace.
        </p>
        <p>
          Refunds are at our discretion. A refund goes back to the card that
          paid, and the amount refunded is taken off the balance.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="When the balance runs low">
        <p>
          Below the minimum balance, new calls are refused and campaigns pause
          until you top up. A call already in progress is allowed to finish and
          is still charged, so the balance can go below zero. The next top-up
          covers that first.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Your own providers">
        <p>
          You connect your own accounts for the language model, the voice, the
          transcriber, the knowledge base's embeddings and your phone numbers,
          using your own keys. Those providers bill you directly, under their
          own terms. Our fee covers the platform only.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are responsible for following those providers' terms and for
          their charges, including for calls your agents make. We are not
          responsible for their service or their bills.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Acceptable use">
        <p>Do not use the service to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>make spam calls, or call people who have asked not to be called;</li>
          <li>place automated or prerecorded calls that the law forbids, or without the consent the law requires;</li>
          <li>record calls without the consent the law requires where you or the other person are;</li>
          <li>break the law in any other way, or try to break into or overload the service.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You are responsible for the calls your agents make and answer, and
          for following the calling, recording and privacy laws of each place
          you call.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="The partner program">
        <p>
          {`Partners who build and manage voice agents for clients earn ${formatSharePercent()} of those clients' platform fees. The program is in early access, and how it works is described on `}<a href="/partners" class="link">the partner page</a>.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="No warranty">
        <p>
          The service is provided as it is and as available. We do not promise
          that it will be uninterrupted or free of errors, or that it suits a
          particular purpose. AI agents can say the wrong thing; check what
          yours says before you rely on it.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Limitation of liability">
        <p>
          As far as the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or
          consequential loss, such as lost profit, revenue, data or business.
          Our total liability to you is limited to what you paid us in the 12
          months before the claim. Nothing here limits a liability that the law
          does not allow us to limit.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Ending your account">
        <p>
          You can stop using the service at any time and ask us to close your
          account. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms,
          and we will tell you why by email unless the law stops us.
        </p>
        <p>
          When an account closes, its data is deleted as described in
          the <a href="/privacy" class="link">privacy policy</a>. Unused credit is
          not refunded automatically; ask us, and the refund rules above apply.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection heading="Changes to these terms">
        <p>
          We may change these terms. When we do, we will update the version and
          date at the top of this page, email account owners, and ask you to
          accept the new terms before you carry on using the service.
        </p>
      </LegalSection>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
